I am blown away by Opus 5.5, I use the model for almost any task and it always delivers (only my AI agents still run on Grok). I have not hit my token limits once over the past weeks, despite building and testing software. Opus 5.5 is friendly, smart and fast. Also for legal stuff it’s better than any previous model (okay, Fable is likely even better, but I don’t want to pay for usage tokens anymore). 

AI models made incredible progress over the past weeks. I am now at the point that I feel I don’t need better models anymore for 99% of the tasks I give it, which means that hardly anybody will need frontier models anymore.  I wonder what implications that will have for Anthropic and OpenAI. Will training become less important and will the focus be on inference? We live in incredible times, but most people have no clue (96% of Americans don’t even pay for AI, and of course they do not use agents either).

